From 0bb6fd04640a3007aea3a286526d1f732b17f558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:38:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sampling: Gumbel-max dist pick, and MTP drafts picked with a
 copy of the target's chain

The dist sampler picks argmax_i p_i / E_i, with E_i = -log(u_i) and u_i a hash of
(seed, accepted count, token id). This is an exact sample of p, as the inverse-CDF
pick was. The noise of a token does not depend on which other tokens are candidates.

The MTP drafter now picks each draft token with a clone of the target's sampler chain
(dparams.chain_tgt). The clone has the target's seed and accepted count, so draft token
j draws the same noise as row j of the verify. For a sampled request, draft and target
then pick the same token more often. Verify is still an exact match, so the output is
the target's sample whatever was drafted.

dist has no backend implementation now: ggml has no op to hash the candidates' ids.
With --backend-sampling the chain before dist still runs on the device; the pick runs
on the CPU over the top-k candidates. The draft's backend top-k goes from 10 to 40 so
that the copy of the target's chain (top-k 20) has its candidates.

Port of Strata PR #1281 (6381df3, STRATA_SPEC_GUMBEL).

