+// The pick is argmax_i p_i / E_i, with E_i = -log(u_i) ~ Exp(1). This is the Gumbel-max trick: the pick is an exact
+// sample of p. u_i is a hash of (seed, n_accept, token id). The noise of a token therefore does not depend on which
+// other tokens are candidates, or on their order. A draft that runs a copy of this sampler on its own logits gives
+// each token the same noise as the target does at that position, so draft and target agree more often.
+// The counter moves on accept, not on apply: a position sampled twice (a verify row, then a replay) gets the same noise.
 struct llama_sampler_dist : public llama_sampler_backend {
